💡 severity: SUGGESTION —
💡 **SUGGESTION: `layer: project` with a null `projectDir` silently targets the wrong file**

With `AppContextCapSource.project` and `projectDir == null`, this line interpolates to the literal path `null/.fah/config.yaml`, and the `ConfigService` env below falls back to `cwd: home` — so the "project-layer" set would silently land in the **user** file while the caller asked for the project layer (and the remove path would touch a `null/.fah/config.yaml` path). A wrong-scope write is exactly the failure mode this feature exists to avoid.

No current caller can hit it: `ContextWindowCapSection._writeLayer` only picks the project layer when `widget.projectDir != null`. But `writeAppContextWindowCap` is a public service API — a cheap guard keeps the contract honest:

```dart
if (layer == AppContextCapSource.project && projectDir == null) {
  throw ArgumentError('layer project requires a projectDir');
}
```

